      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T13:27:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. I considered the following approaches:\n\n- I could maintain the state here, but then the state had to be shared between the two methods (`onDexoptStart` and `onDexoptTargetResult`) so it would have to be a class member of `PrimaryDexopter`, making the class stateful. Currently, none of `Dexopter` and its derived classes is stateful, so I don\u0027t want to make it stateful just for this.\n\n- `Dexopter` (the base class) only calls the hooks and doesn\u0027t know about SDM files, so I can\u0027t explicitly maintain the state there.\n\n- I could have `Dexopter` hold an opaque object to maintain the state and pass it among the hooks, and them have `PrimaryDexopter` mutate the object, but that sounds like overengineering for this problem.\n\nI suggest to leave it as is since dexopt is not performance critical.",
      "parentUuid": "c8a38fed_826dc393",
